## Rebuilding Packages from Source

OpenHPC packages can be rebuilt from source using the source {% if is_ubuntu
%}packages{% else %}RPMs{% endif %} available from
the OpenHPC repository. This allows administrators to customize package builds
for their specific needs. {% if is_ubuntu %}One way to accomplish this is to
enable the source repository, download the Debian source package, and rebuild it
locally. A brief example using the FFTW library is highlighted below.

```bash
# Enable OpenHPC source packages
OHPC_REPO_ROOT="{{ ohpc_repo_server }}{{ ohpc_repo_path }}"
OHPC_UBUNTU_REPO="${OHPC_REPO_ROOT}/Ubuntu_24.04"
OHPC_KEYRING="{{ ohpc_apt_keyring }}"
echo "deb-src [signed-by=${OHPC_KEYRING}] ${OHPC_UBUNTU_REPO}/ ./" \
	> /etc/apt/sources.list.d/versatushpc-openhpc-src.list
apt update

# Install Debian packaging tools and FFTW build dependencies
sudo apt -y install build-essential debhelper devscripts fakeroot
sudo apt -y build-dep fftw-gnu15-openmpi5-ohpc

# Download source package from the OpenHPC repository
apt source fftw-gnu15-openmpi5-ohpc
cd fftw-gnu15-openmpi5-ohpc-*

# Modify Debian packaging or source as desired, then record a local revision
dch --local +local "Local FFTW rebuild"

# Rebuild binary packages and install the local package
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
sudo apt -y install ../fftw-gnu15-openmpi5-ohpc_*_*.deb
```
{% else %}One way to accomplish this is to install the
appropriate source RPM, modify the spec file as needed, and rebuild to obtain an
updated binary RPM. OpenHPC spec files contain macros to facilitate local
customizations of compiler, compilation flags and MPI family. A brief example
using the FFTW library is highlighted below.  Note that the source RPMs can be
downloaded from the community repository server at [{{ ohpc_repo_server }}]({{
ohpc_repo_server }}) via a web browser or directly via dnf as highlighted below.
In this example we make an explicit change to FFTW's configuration, as well as
modifying the CFLAGS environment variable. The package is also tagged with an
additional delimiter to allow easy co-installation and use.

```bash
# Install rpm-build package and dnf tools from base OS distro
sudo dnf -y install rpm-build dnf-plugins-core

# Install FFTW's build dependencies
sudo dnf builddep fftw-gnu15-openmpi5-ohpc

# Download SRPM from OpenHPC repository and install locally
dnf download --source fftw-gnu15-openmpi5-ohpc
rpm -i ./fftw-gnu15-openmpi5-ohpc-*.rpm

# Modify spec file as desired
cd ~/rpmbuild/SPECS
sed -i "s/enable-static=no/enable-static=yes/" fftw.spec

# Increment RPM release so the package manager will see an update
sed -i "s/Release:   400.ohpc.3.1/Release:   400.ohpc.3.2/" fftw.spec

# Rebuild binary RPM. Note that additional directives can be specified to modify build
rpmbuild -bb --define "OHPC_CFLAGS '-O3 -mtune=native'" \
        --define "OHPC_CUSTOM_DELIM static" fftw.spec

# Install the new package
sudo dnf -y install \
        ../RPMS/$(uname -m)/fftw-gnu15-openmpi5-static-ohpc-*.$(uname -m).rpm

```

The new module file now appears along side the default.
```console
$ module -t spider fftw
fftw/3.3.10-static
fftw/3.3.10
```
{% endif %}
